relaxed_d3_egg.multi.pb  -- SAVED multi-output rewrite rules (gitignored: 164 MB > GitHub limit)

Contents: 798,729 multi-output rules (RuleCollection protobuf; every rule has
len(mappedOutput) > 1, so its dst graph produces several outputs -- typically via a
`split`, whose outputs are selected by split_0/split_1). These have NO single-pattern
egg form and belong to tensat's multi-pattern lane (rewrites.rs PRE_DEFINED_MULTI), not
the single-pattern --rules file. pb2egg.py saves them here instead of dropping them
(--multi-out); the multi-pattern conversion will be built against this file later.

Load:  import rules_pb2; rc = rules_pb2.RuleCollection()
       rc.ParseFromString(open("relaxed_d3_egg.multi.pb","rb").read())   # -> 798729 rules

Regenerate (this .pb + relaxed_d3_graph_subst.pb + all text artifacts):
       sbatch ... apptainer exec tensat.sif bash NNs/run_rule_gen.sh
Both large .pb files live durably on gscratch; only their text derivatives
(relaxed_d3_{dedup,verified,core}.txt) are tracked in git.
